<title>USA: Castle says knows no reason for stock fall.</title>
<headline>Castle says knows no reason for stock fall.</headline>
<dateline>JERSEY CITY, N.J. 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Castle Convertible Fund Inc said on Tuesday it knows of no reason why its stock fell precipitously.</p>
<p>Castle shares were down 7-1/4 to 16-3/4 by mid-afternoon Tuesday.</p>
<p>David Alger, Castle's president, said in a statement that the company is a closed-end convertible bond fund with a net asset value of $27.76 as of last Friday.  Alger said there was no significant impairment on Friday in the value of the fund, and that it is presently paying a $0.37 income dividend on a quarterly basis.</p>
</text>
